WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
Long range: how do you play balls three steps away or even further?

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.560
This is long range: after the run you can still load and adjust.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.840
This is even further: sprint flat out and make getting the ball back the priority.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.708
For far balls, don't take the racket back and then run dragging it along.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000 line:5%
Common mistake

00:00:14.708 --> 00:00:17.400
That badly slows you down and you won't get there in time.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.840
The right way: first sprint with big steps to get close to the ball quickly.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:29.401
Once you're within the three-step middle distance from the last lesson, take the racket back as you run,

00:00:29.401 --> 00:00:32.050
and settle briefly to load before you hit.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:38.090
You can think of this movement simply as a few big sprint steps plus taking the racket back as you go.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.010
Load, hit.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:48.507
For balls even further away, you can only sprint flat out; there may be no room to load and adjust,

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:50.270
and you hit in the air while running.

